---
description: Automatic Toast Integration for Forms, Tables, and Actions using Sonner
globs:
[
  "features/**/form/**/*.tsx",
  "features/**/table/**/*.tsx",
  "features/**/api/**/*.ts",
  "features/**/components/**/*.tsx"
]
alwaysApply: true
---

# Toast Integration System

All user-triggered actions MUST automatically trigger toast notifications using:

import { toast } from "@/components/ui/sonner"

---

# Global Setup

Toaster is already initialized in app/layout.tsx.

Rules:

- Do NOT create additional Toaster instances
- Do NOT override global Toaster configuration
- Always use the global Toaster

---

# Core Principle

Toast must be:

- automatic
- consistent
- tied to user actions
- impossible to forget

---

# Form Integration (REQUIRED)

All forms MUST use toast.promise on submit.

Pattern:

onSubmit: async (values) => {
return toast.promise(submit(values), {
loading: "Saving...",
success: "Saved successfully",
error: "Failed to save"
})
}

Rules:

- MUST use toast.promise
- MUST include loading, success, and error
- MUST NOT use try/catch without toast

---

# Create / Update Message Standard

Create → "Created successfully"  
Update → "Updated successfully"  
Save → "Saved successfully"

---

# Table Row Actions (REQUIRED)

All row actions MUST use toast.promise.

Pattern:

toast.promise(deleteItem(id), {
loading: "Deleting...",
success: "Deleted successfully",
error: "Failed to delete"
})

Applies to:

- delete
- update status
- duplicate
- activate / deactivate

---

# Bulk Actions (REQUIRED)

All bulk actions MUST show toast.

Pattern:

toast.promise(bulkDelete(ids), {
loading: `Deleting ${ids.length} items...`,
success: "Bulk delete successful",
error: "Bulk delete failed"
})

---

# Toggle / Status Update

Use either:

toast.success("Status updated")

OR

toast.promise(updateStatus(), {
loading: "Updating...",
success: "Status updated",
error: "Failed to update status"
})

---

# API Layer Rule

API functions MUST throw errors.

Example:

export async function createMaterial(data) {
const res = await fetch(...)

if (!res.ok) {
throw new Error("Create failed")
}

return res.json()
}

Rules:

- Do NOT use toast inside API layer
- Toast MUST be handled in UI layer

---

# CSV Import Integration

Must support:

Success:
toast.success("Import completed")

Partial:
toast.warning("Some rows failed to import")

Error:
toast.error("Import failed")

---

# CSV Export Integration

Pattern:

toast.success("Export started")

Optional:

toast.success("Export completed")

---

# Long Running Process

Use toast.promise.

Pattern:

toast.promise(processData(), {
loading: "Processing...",
success: "Process completed",
error: "Process failed"
})

---

# No Changes Case

If no changes detected:

toast.warning("No changes detected")

---

# Delete Confirmation Pattern

Flow:

1. confirm dialog
2. execute action
3. toast

Pattern:

if (!confirm("Delete this item?")) return

toast.promise(deleteItem(id), {
loading: "Deleting...",
success: "Deleted successfully",
error: "Failed to delete"
})

---

# Error Message Rules

Errors MUST:

- be human-readable
- be short
- avoid technical details

Bad:
"500 Internal Server Error"

Good:
"Failed to save data"

---

# UX Rules

- One action → one toast
- Avoid duplicate toasts
- Use promise toast for async
- Keep message under 60 characters

---

# Naming Convention

Use consistent messages:

Created successfully  
Updated successfully  
Deleted successfully  
Saved successfully  
Failed to save  
Failed to delete

---

# Forbidden

Do NOT:

- use alert()
- forget toast in user actions
- show raw error messages
- duplicate toast calls
- use other toast libraries
- create custom toast systems

---

# Goal

All user actions must have:

- clear feedback
- consistent UX
- non-blocking notification
- enterprise-grade behavior
